{"path": "index.html", "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<meta name="description" content="Why Is the Sky Blue? — one question, three answers, in English and Simplified Chinese.">
<title>Why Is the Sky Blue? · 为什么天空是蓝色的？</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --ink: #1c2b47;
    --body: #3a4a67;
    --muted: #71809b;
    --line: #d9e5f2;
    --hair: #eef4fb;
    --accent: #1265c9;
    --accent-soft: #e9f2fd;
    --en-tag: #0e62b4;
    --zh-tag: #c2571d;
  }
  *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial,
      "PingFang SC", "Hiragino Sans GB", "Microsoft YaHei", "Noto Sans SC", sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: #f4f8fd;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  ::selection { background: #cfe4fb; }

  /* ---------- Hero ---------- */
  .hero {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    text-align: center;
    color: #fff;
    padding: 84px 24px 110px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(1200px 480px at 50% 118%, rgba(255,190,90,.35), transparent 62%),
      linear-gradient(180deg, #081c46 0%, #14418c 34%, #3d86cf 68%, #a8d4f2 92%, #d9eefc 100%);
  }
  .hero .sun {
    position: absolute;
    left: 50%; bottom: -130px;
    width: 260px; height: 260px;
    margin-left: -130px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 40% 35%, #fff9e3 0%, #ffe066 35%, #ffb340 62%, rgba(255,140,60,0) 76%);
    filter: drop-shadow(0 0 55px rgba(255,190,80,.55));
  }
  .cloud {
    position: absolute;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.16);
    border-radius: 999px;
    animation: drift 10s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  }
  .cloud.c1 { width: 240px; height: 44px; top: 36%; left: 7%;  filter: blur(7px); }
  .cloud.c2 { width: 320px; height: 52px; top: 20%; right: 5%; filter: blur(9px); animation-delay: -5s; }
  @keyframes drift { from { transform: translateX(-16px); } to { transform: translateX(16px); } }
  .hero h1 { position: relative; margin: 0; }
  .hero h1 .en {
    display: block;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .01em;
    text-shadow: 0 2px 18px rgba(6,30,80,.35);
  }
  .hero h1 .zh {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 10px;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3vw, 1.8rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    opacity: .93;
  }
  .tagline {
    position: relative;
    margin: 20px auto 0;
    max-width: 760px;
    font-size: 1.02rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    opacity: .9;
  }
  .tagline .zh { display: block; margin-top: 6px; font-size: .98rem; }

  /* ---------- Toolbar ---------- */
  .toolbar {
    position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 50;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.86);
    backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(12px);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
  .toolbar .inner {
    max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto;
    display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 14px; flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: 10px 20px;
  }
  .seg {
    display: flex;
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 4px;
    gap: 2px;
  }
  .seg button {
    border: 0; background: transparent;
    padding: 7px 15px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    font: inherit; font-size: .88rem; font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background .15s ease, color .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease;
  }
  .seg button.active {
    background: #fff;
    color: var(--accent);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 4px rgba(16,60,120,.18);
  }
  .chips { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .chip {
    display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px;
    padding: 7px 13px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--body);
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: .88rem; font-weight: 600;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    background: #fff;
    transition: all .15s ease;
  }
  .chip:hover { border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--accent); }
  .chip.active { background: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: #fff; }

  /* ---------- Layout ---------- */
  main { max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 34px 20px 40px; }
  .colhead {
    display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; column-gap: 24px;
    padding: 2px 8px 12px;
  }
  .colhead span {
    font-size: .72rem; font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .colhead .en { color: var(--en-tag); padding-right: 22px; }
  .colhead .zh { color: var(--zh-tag); padding-left: 22px; }

  .deck {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 16px;
    box-shadow: 0 12px 32px rgba(21,58,116,.08);
    margin-bottom: 26px;
    overflow: hidden;
    scroll-margin-top: 92px;
  }
  .deck::before {
    content: ""; display: block; height: 5px;
    background: var(--deck-grad, linear-gradient(90deg, #7fd4ff, #4aa3df));
  }
  #kid  { --deck-grad: linear-gradient(90deg, #8fdcff, #4aa3df); }
  #teen { --deck-grad: linear-gradient(90deg, #ffd36b, #ff9d3c); }
  #phd  { --deck-grad: linear-gradient(90deg, #8b5cf6, #3b82f6); }
  .deck-inner { padding: 4px 30px 14px; }

  .pair {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: 24px;
    padding: 16px 0;
  }
  .pair + .pair { border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .cell { min-width: 0; }
  .cell.en { border-right: 1px dashed var(--line); padding-right: 22px; }
  .cell.zh { padding-left: 22px; }

  .pair p { margin: 0; line-height: 1.78; font-size: .98rem; color: var(--body); }
  .pair h2 { font-size: 1.68rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: 12px 0 0; font-weight: 800; }
  .pair h3 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 4px 0 0; font-weight: 700; }
  .pair ul, .pair ol { margin: 4px 0 0; padding-left: 1.25em; }
  .pair li { line-height: 1.72; font-size: .98rem; color: var(--body); margin: 7px 0; }
  .pair li::marker { color: var(--accent); }
  strong { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 700; }
  .formula {
    background: var(--accent-soft);
    border: 1px solid #d5e6fb;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    margin: 8px 0 0;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: "STIX Two Math", "Cambria Math", "Times New Roman", Georgia, serif;
    font-size: 1.03rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }

  /* ---------- Language modes ---------- */
  body.mode-en .cell.zh, body.mode-zh .cell.en { display: none; }
  body.mode-en .pair, body.mode-zh .pair {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 46rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
    column-gap: 0;
  }
  body.mode-en .cell.en, body.mode-zh .cell.zh {
    border-right: 0; padding-left: 0; padding-right: 0;
  }
  body.mode-en .colhead, body.mode-zh .colhead {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 46rem);
    margin: 0 auto;
    column-gap: 0;
  }
  body.mode-en .colhead .zh { display: none; }
  body.mode-en .colhead .en { padding-right: 0; }
  body.mode-zh .colhead .en { display: none; }
  body.mode-zh .colhead .zh { padding-left: 0; }
  body.mode-en .hero h1 .zh, body.mode-en .tagline .zh { display: none; }
  body.mode-zh .hero h1 .en, body.mode-zh .tagline .en { display: none; }

  footer {
    max-width: 1240px; margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 6px 20px 48px;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: .85rem;
    text-align: center;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  kbd {
    background: #fff;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-bottom-width: 2px;
    border-radius: 5px;
    padding: 1px 6px;
    font-family: inherit;
    font-size: .78rem;
  }

  /* ---------- Narrow screens: stack languages ---------- */
  @media (max-width: 880px) {
    .pair { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; column-gap: 0 !important; }
    .cell.en {
      border-right: 0; padding-right: 0;
      border-bottom: 1px dashed var(--line);
      padding-bottom: 12px;
    }
    .cell.zh { padding-left: 0; padding-top: 12px; }
    body.mode-en .cell.en, body.mode-zh .cell.en { border-bottom: 0; padding-bottom: 0; }
    .colhead { display: none; }
    .deck-inner { padding: 2px 18px 12px; }
    .hero { padding: 60px 18px 88px; }
  }

  /* ---------- Print ---------- */
  @media print {
    .toolbar { display: none; }
    .hero { padding: 28px 18px; }
    .deck { box-shadow: none; break-inside: avoid; }
    body { background: #fff; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body class="mode-both">

<header class="hero">
  <div class="cloud c1" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="cloud c2" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <div class="sun" aria-hidden="true"></div>
  <h1>
    <span class="en" lang="en">Why Is the Sky Blue?</span>
    <span class="zh" lang="zh-CN">为什么天空是蓝色的？</span>
  </h1>
  <p class="tagline">
    <span class="en" lang="en">One question, three answers — tuned for a toddler, a teenager, and a physicist.</span>
    <span class="zh" lang="zh-CN">同一个问题，三种回答——分别为 3 岁幼童、高中生和物理学家量身打造。</span>
  </p>
</header>

<nav class="toolbar" aria-label="Presentation controls">
  <div class="inner">
    <div class="seg" role="group" aria-label="Language display">
      <button data-mode="both" class="active" aria-pressed="true">双语 Both</button>
      <button data-mode="en" aria-pressed="false">EN</button>
      <button data-mode="zh" aria-pressed="false">中文 ZH</button>
    </div>
    <div class="chips" role="group" aria-label="Sections">
      <a class="chip" href="#kid">🌈 <span lang="en">3-Year-Old</span> · <span lang="zh-CN">小朋友</span></a>
      <a class="chip" href="#teen">🎒 <span lang="en">High School</span> · <span lang="zh-CN">高中生</span></a>
      <a class="chip" href="#phd">⚛️ <span lang="en">Physics PhD</span> · <span lang="zh-CN">物理博士</span></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>

<main>
  <div class="colhead" aria-hidden="true">
    <span class="en" lang="en">English</span>
    <span class="zh" lang="zh-CN">简体中文</span>
  </div>

  <!-- ================= 3-YEAR-OLD ================= -->
  <section class="deck" id="kid" aria-labelledby="kid-title">
    <div class="deck-inner">
      <div class="pair">
        <h2 class="en" id="kid-title" lang="en">🌈 For a 3-year-old</h2>
        <h2 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">🌈 写给 3 岁小朋友</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Look up! What color is the sky? Blue! But how does the sky get its color?</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">抬头看！天空是什么颜色的？蓝色！可是，天空是怎么变成这个颜色的呢？</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The Sun is like a big flashlight that shines <strong>rainbow paint</strong> — its light is secretly all the colors of the rainbow mixed up together. And the air all around us is full of <strong>super-tiny, super-tiny things</strong> that are too little for you to see, even with the best eyes you have.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">太阳就像一支大大的手电筒，洒出<strong>彩虹色的颜料</strong>——它的光其实是所有彩虹颜色悄悄混在一起的。而我们周围的空气里，藏着<strong>超级超级小的东西</strong>，它们太小了，即使用你最棒的眼睛也看不见。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">When the Sun's paint hits those tiny things, the light bounces around. Some colors are really good at bouncing around, and some are not so good:</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">当太阳的颜料碰到那些小东西时，光就开始弹来弹去。有些颜色特别会弹，有些就不太会：</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ul class="en" lang="en">
          <li><strong>Blue light is the bounciest</strong> — like the bounciest ball on the playground.</li>
          <li><strong>Red and yellow light are a bit lazy</strong> — they mostly just keep going straight.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li><strong>蓝光最爱弹来弹去</strong>——就像操场上跳得最高最欢的小球。</li>
          <li><strong>红光和黄光有点懒</strong>——它们大多只管直直地往前走。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">So when you look up, the blue light that bounced around in the air is the color you see. That's why the sky is blue!</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">所以当你抬头看的时候，在空气里弹来弹去的蓝光，就是你能看到的颜色。这就是天空是蓝色的原因！</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">And at <strong>sunset</strong>, the Sun's light has to travel through a <em>lot</em> more air to get to you. All the bouncy blue light gets bounced away before it reaches your eyes, and the lazy red and orange light gets to arrive — that's why sunsets are orange! 🌅</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">而在<strong>日落</strong>的时候，太阳光要穿过<em>厚得多</em>的空气才能到达你身边。那些爱弹来弹去的蓝光在到达你眼睛之前就被弹走了，而懒洋洋的红光和橙光却一路走到了你的眼睛里——所以日落是橙色的！🌅</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= HIGH SCHOOL ================= -->
  <section class="deck" id="teen" aria-labelledby="teen-title">
    <div class="deck-inner">
      <div class="pair">
        <h2 class="en" id="teen-title" lang="en">🎒 For a High School Student</h2>
        <h2 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">🎒 写给高中生</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en"><strong>The short version:</strong> Sunlight is white (all colors mixed together). The molecules in the air scatter short-wavelength light — blue and violet — much more strongly than long-wavelength light. That scattered blue light, coming from <em>every direction</em>, is what you see when you look up.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN"><strong>简短版：</strong>太阳光是白色的（所有颜色混在一起）。空气中的分子对短波长的光——蓝光和紫光——的散射，远比对长波长的光强得多。从<em>四面八方</em>散射而来的蓝光，正是你抬头时看到的东西。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Here's the full story:</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">完整的故事是这样的：</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">1. Sunlight contains all the colors</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">1. 太阳光包含所有颜色</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Sunlight looks white, but it's a mix of every visible wavelength, ~400 nm (violet) to ~700 nm (red). Run it through a prism (or a raindrop) and you get a rainbow.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">太阳光看起来是白色的，但它其实是所有可见波长的混合，大约从 400 nm（紫色）到 700 nm（红色）。让光穿过三棱镜（或一颗雨滴），你就会得到一道彩虹。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">2. The air is full of tiny scattering centers</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">2. 空气里到处都是微小的散射中心</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The atmosphere is mostly N₂ and O₂ molecules, each about 0.3 nm wide. That's <em>thousands of times smaller</em> than the wavelength of visible light. When a light wave hits a molecule, its electric field makes the molecule's electron cloud wiggle, and a wiggling charge re-emits light — it <strong>scatters</strong> the light in all directions. This is called <strong>Rayleigh scattering</strong> (named after Lord Rayleigh).</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">大气主要由 N₂ 和 O₂ 分子组成，每个分子宽约 0.3 nm，比可见光的波长<em>小几千倍</em>。当光波遇到一个分子时，光的电场会让分子中的电子云抖动起来，而抖动的电荷会再次辐射出光——光就这样被向四面八方<strong>散射</strong>开了。这叫<strong>瑞利散射</strong>（以瑞利勋爵的名字命名）。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">3. Shorter wavelengths scatter way more</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">3. 波长越短，散射越强</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The scattered power scales with the <em>fourth power</em> of frequency, or inversely with the fourth power of wavelength:</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">散射功率正比于频率的<em>四次方</em>，也即与波长的四次方成反比：</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <div class="formula en" lang="en"><strong>Scattered intensity ∝ 1 / λ⁴</strong></div>
        <div class="formula zh" lang="zh-CN"><strong>散射强度 ∝ 1 / λ⁴</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">That's a brutally steep dependence. Blue light (~450 nm) is scattered about (650/450)⁴ ≈ <strong>4–5× more</strong> than red light (~650 nm). So as sunlight streams through the atmosphere, blue gets continually bounced out of the beam and sent in <em>all</em> directions. When you look up, you're seeing blue light that was scattered from the Sun by the air between you and the top of the atmosphere — from every direction at once.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">这是一个极其陡峭的依赖关系。蓝光（约 450 nm）的散射强度比红光（约 650 nm）强大约 (650/450)⁴ ≈ <strong>4–5 倍</strong>。于是当阳光穿过大气时，蓝光不断被弹射出直射光束、朝<em>所有</em>方向飞散。你抬头看到的，正是太阳光被你和大气顶层之间的空气散射后、同时从四面八方抵达的蓝光。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">4. So why isn't the sky violet?</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">4. 那为什么天空不是紫色的？</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Violet (~400 nm) is scattered even more than blue, so you'd think the sky should look violet. Three reasons it doesn't:</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">紫光（约 400 nm）的散射比蓝光还强，照理说天空应该看起来是紫色的。它不是，原因有三：</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ol class="en" lang="en">
          <li><strong>The Sun emits less violet</strong> — its spectrum (roughly a 5,800 K blackbody) falls off toward the UV.</li>
          <li><strong>Your eye is bad at violet</strong> — the short-wavelength (S) cones are a small fraction of your cones, and violet also triggers the red/green cones, which muddies the color.</li>
          <li><strong>The colors mix</strong> — the violet, blue, and a bit of green scattered from different parts of the sky blend into the "azure" chromaticity we call blue.</li>
        </ol>
        <ol class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li><strong>太阳发出的紫光较少</strong>——太阳光谱（近似 5,800 K 的黑体谱）向紫外端逐渐衰减。</li>
          <li><strong>人眼对紫色不敏感</strong>——对短波长敏感的视锥细胞（S 型视锥细胞）在全部视锥细胞中占比很小，而且紫光还会同时刺激红/绿视锥细胞，使颜色显得发浑。</li>
          <li><strong>各种颜色混合</strong>——天空不同区域散射出的紫光、蓝光和少量绿光混合在一起，形成了我们称为蓝色（“蔚蓝”）的色度。</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">5. Sunsets: the same physics, longer road</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">5. 日落：同一套物理规律，更长的路程</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">At noon the Sun is high, and light travels a short path through the atmosphere. At sunset it travels through ~10–30× more air (the "airmass"). Along that long path, nearly all the blue is scattered <em>out</em> of the direct beam — leaving red, orange, and yellow to reach your eyes. Same 1/λ⁴ law, just more of it.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">正午时太阳高悬，光线穿过大气层的路程很短。日落时，光要多穿过约 10–30 倍的空气（“大气质量”，airmass）。在这条漫长路径上，几乎全部蓝光都被散射<em>出</em>了直射光束——只剩下红光、橙光和黄光能到达你的眼睛。还是同一条 1/λ⁴ 规律，只是作用的路径更长了。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Bonus facts</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">附加小知识</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ul class="en" lang="en">
          <li>The scattered sky light is <strong>partially polarized</strong> — at 90° from the Sun it's almost fully polarized. Rotate a pair of polarizing sunglasses and the sky darkens/brightens depending on the direction you look.</li>
          <li><strong>Clouds are white</strong> because water droplets are <em>huge</em> compared to light's wavelength (~20,000–200,000× bigger). They scatter all colors equally (Mie scattering), so clouds look white.</li>
          <li>An astronaut in space (outside the atmosphere) sees a <strong>black</strong> sky, even at noon — no air, no scattering.</li>
          <li>On <strong>Mars</strong>, the sky is butterscotch/pink with a bluish sun, because its fine dust scatters differently. On <strong>Jupiter</strong>, it's yellowish, due to haze particles of a completely different size.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li>天空的散射光<strong>部分偏振</strong>——在与太阳成 90° 的方向上，它几乎是完全偏振的。转动一副偏光太阳镜，天空会随你看的方向变暗或变亮。</li>
          <li><strong>云是白色的</strong>，因为水滴相对于光的波长来说<em>非常大</em>（大 2 万到 20 万倍）。它对所有颜色的光散射程度相同（米氏散射），所以云看起来是白的。</li>
          <li>在太空（大气层之外）的宇航员，即使在正午也看到<strong>黑色</strong>的天空——没有空气，就没有散射。</li>
          <li>在<strong>火星</strong>上，天空呈奶黄色/粉色，太阳偏蓝——因为那里细密的尘埃散射行为不同。在<strong>木星</strong>上，天空偏黄——那里的霾粒子尺寸完全不同。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ================= PHYSICS PHD ================= -->
  <section class="deck" id="phd" aria-labelledby="phd-title">
    <div class="deck-inner">
      <div class="pair">
        <h2 class="en" id="phd-title" lang="en">⚛️ For a Physics PhD</h2>
        <h2 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">⚛️ 写给物理学博士</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Microscopic mechanism</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">微观机制</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The atmosphere is in the deep Rayleigh regime: molecular size a ≈ 0.29 nm (N₂) gives a size parameter x = 2πa/λ ~ 10⁻³ for visible λ, far below the x ≪ 1 condition. The incident field induces a molecular dipole p = αE (for air, Re α ≈ 1.8–1.9 × 10⁻⁴⁰ C·m²/V), and the re-radiation from an oscillating dipole scales as P ∝ ω⁴|α|²|E₀|² (dipole radiation in the non-resonant limit, where α is essentially frequency-independent across the visible since we are far from the UV resonances). This gives the differential cross section</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">大气处于深度瑞利区：分子尺寸 a ≈ 0.29 nm（N₂），对可见光波长 λ，尺寸参数 x = 2πa/λ ~ 10⁻³，深度满足 x ≪ 1 条件。入射场感应出分子偶极矩 p = αE（对空气，Re α ≈ 1.8–1.9 × 10⁻⁴⁰ C·m²/V），振荡偶极子的再辐射功率按 P ∝ ω⁴|α|²|E₀|² 标度（非谐振极限下的偶极子辐射；由于远离紫外共振，极化率 α 在整个可见光范围内基本不随频率变化）。由此得到微分截面</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <div class="formula en" lang="en">dσ/dΩ = (3σ/8π)(1 + cos²θ), &nbsp; σ = (8π³/3)·α²/(ε₀²λ⁴)</div>
        <div class="formula zh" lang="zh-CN">dσ/dΩ = (3σ/8π)(1 + cos²θ), &nbsp; σ = (8π³/3)·α²/(ε₀²λ⁴)</div>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">up to a small depolarization factor (6+3p)/(6−7p) ≈ 1.03 for linear molecules, and yields the familiar σ ∝ λ⁻⁴. (Equivalently, via Clausius–Mossotti, σ = (8π³/3)·((n²−1)/(n²+2))²·λ⁻⁴/N², where n − 1 ≈ 2.8×10⁻⁴ for air.)</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">对线性分子还有一个小量级的退偏振因子 (6+3p)/(6−7p) ≈ 1.03，并给出熟悉的 σ ∝ λ⁻⁴。（等价地，由克劳修斯–莫索蒂关系可得 σ = (8π³/3)·((n²−1)/(n²+2))²·λ⁻⁴/N²，其中空气的 n − 1 ≈ 2.8×10⁻⁴。）</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Numbers that matter</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">关键数值</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ul class="en" lang="en">
          <li>σ_R(air, 550 nm) ≈ 4 × 10⁻³¹ m² (∝ λ⁻⁴)</li>
          <li>Vertical column: N_col = P/(mg) ≈ 3.57 × 10⁵ mol·m⁻² ≈ 2.15 × 10²⁹ molecules·m⁻² (≈ 10.3 t/m²)</li>
          <li>Rayleigh optical depth (sea level, standard atmosphere): <strong>τ_R(400/450/550/700 nm) ≈ 0.31 / 0.19 / 0.085 / 0.033</strong></li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li>σ_R（空气，550 nm）≈ 4 × 10⁻³¹ m²（∝ λ⁻⁴）</li>
          <li>垂直气柱：N_col = P/(mg) ≈ 3.57 × 10⁵ mol·m⁻² ≈ 2.15 × 10²⁹ 分子·m⁻²（≈ 10.3 t/m²）</li>
          <li>瑞利光学厚度（海平面、标准大气）：<strong>τ_R(400/450/550/700 nm) ≈ 0.31 / 0.19 / 0.085 / 0.033</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Since τ ≪ 1 over all but slant paths, the daylight sky is overwhelmingly a <strong>single-scattering radiance field</strong>: L_sky(λ, θ) ≈ L_sun(λ)·(dτ/dΩ)(θ)·g(μ_sun), with g of order unity (slant-path geometry). A quick energy check: τ·F_sun ∼ 0.1 × 1360 W/m² ≈ 100+ W/m² of scattered visible power, consistent with measured clear-sky diffuse irradiances (~5–10% of the total).</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">除了斜射（长路径）情形，处处 τ ≪ 1，因此白昼天空几乎完全是<strong>单次散射辐亮度场</strong>：L_sky(λ, θ) ≈ L_sun(λ)·(dτ/dΩ)(θ)·g(μ_sun)，其中 g 是数量级为 1 的因子（由斜射路径的几何关系决定）。快速能量核算：τ·F_sun ∼ 0.1 × 1360 W/m² ≈ 100+ W/m² 的可见光散射功率，与实测的晴空漫射辐照度（约为总辐照度的 5–10%）一致。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Why the chromaticity is "azure," not "violet"</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">为什么色度是“蔚蓝”而非“紫色”</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The sky's spectral radiance at nadir is roughly L_sun(λ)·τ(λ)·(dσ/dΩ)/4π, i.e. ∝ F_sun(λ)/λ⁴ weighted by geometry. Three factors conspire against violet:</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">天底方向天空的光谱辐亮度大致为 L_sun(λ)·τ(λ)·(dσ/dΩ)/4π，即 ∝ F_sun(λ)/λ⁴（带几何权重）。三个因素共同压制了紫色：</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ol class="en" lang="en">
          <li><strong>Solar source function</strong>: F_sun falls toward the UV (Planck at T ≈ 5,778 K, peak at 501 nm); F(400 nm) is ~30% below F(450 nm).</li>
          <li><strong>Observer</strong>: CIE V(400)/V(450) ≈ 0.04/0.32 ≈ 0.12; S-cones are a minority of the cone population, and L/M cone cross-talk dilutes the purple.</li>
          <li><strong>Spectral mixing</strong>: scattered violet from the upper atmosphere, blue and green from lower layers, plus a ~τ² correction from multiple scattering, shift the chromaticity away from spectral violet toward the "blue" of perception.</li>
        </ol>
        <ol class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li><strong>太阳源函数</strong>：F_sun 向紫外端衰减（T ≈ 5,778 K 的普朗克分布，峰值在 501 nm）；F(400 nm) 比 F(450 nm) 低约 30%。</li>
          <li><strong>观测者</strong>：CIE V(400)/V(450) ≈ 0.04/0.32 ≈ 0.12；S 型视锥细胞在视锥细胞中只占少数，L/M 视锥细胞的串扰进一步冲淡了紫色。</li>
          <li><strong>光谱混合</strong>：来自高层大气的散射紫光、来自较低气层的蓝光与绿光，再加上多次散射的 ~τ² 修正项，把色度从光谱紫推向感知上的“蓝”。</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Additionally, the ozone Hartley band (O₃, &lt; 310 nm) makes the atmosphere opaque to the far-UV, so no shorter-wavelength scattered light ever reaches the ground to mix into the sky color.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">此外，臭氧的哈特莱带（O₃，&lt; 310 nm）使大气对远紫外不透明，任何更短波长的散射光都无法到达地面、混入天空的颜色。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Polarization</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">偏振</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">From dσ/dΩ ∝ (1+cos²θ) with the full Stokes formalism, the degree of linear polarization of the scattered beam is ΔP = sin²θ/(1+cos²θ) — 100% at θ = 90° in the ideal Rayleigh limit, oriented perpendicular to the scattering plane. This is directly observable with a polarizer (and was in fact one of the 19th-century confirmations of the dipole model; Rayleigh's own 1899 measurements of polarization and the λ⁻⁴ law settled the molecular-scattering interpretation against Tyndall's colloid hypothesis).</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">由 dσ/dΩ ∝ (1+cos²θ) 结合完整的斯托克斯（Stokes）形式化，散射光束的线偏振度为 ΔP = sin²θ/(1+cos²θ)——在理想瑞利极限下，θ = 90° 时达 100%，偏振方向垂直于散射平面。用偏振片即可直接观测到这一现象（事实上，这正是 19 世纪对偶极子模型的证实之一；瑞利本人 1899 年对偏振与 λ⁻⁴ 规律的测量，最终确立了分子散射的解释，推翻了丁达尔的胶体假说）。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">Sunsets: beam attenuation, not local color</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">日落：是光束衰减，不是局部颜色</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">The redness of the low Sun is <strong>Beer–Lambert attenuation of the direct beam</strong>: T(λ) = e^(−τ(λ)m), where m is the airmass. At a 5° solar elevation, m ≈ 12 (curvature-corrected; the naive 1/μ gives 11.5). Then T(450 nm) = e^(−0.19×12) ≈ 10%, while T(650 nm) = e^(−0.033×12) ≈ 67% — the blue is depleted ~7× more than the red, and the solar disk is correspondingly reddened. Multiple scattering (the τ² term, which backscatters some blue into the beam) and aerosols (AOD adding to τ, with Mie-like angular behavior that can enhance the redness further, e.g. after volcanic eruptions) modulate the effect. The "blue-violet sky + red sun" combination is simply: scattered blue from the short zenithward path, plus a red-depleted direct beam.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">低悬太阳的红色来自<strong>直射光束的比尔–朗伯衰减</strong>：T(λ) = e^(−τ(λ)m)，其中 m 是大气质量（airmass）。太阳高度角为 5° 时，m ≈ 12（经地球曲率修正；简单的 1/μ 公式给出 11.5）。于是 T(450 nm) = e^(−0.19×12) ≈ 10%，而 T(650 nm) = e^(−0.033×12) ≈ 67%——蓝光的衰减程度比红光大 ~7 倍，日面随之变红。多次散射（τ² 项会把一部分蓝光后散射回直射光束中）和气溶胶（气溶胶光学厚度 AOD 叠加进 τ，具有米氏散射般的角分布行为，可进一步加剧红色，例如火山喷发后）会调制这一效应。“蓝紫色天空 + 红色太阳”的组合其实很简单：沿天顶方向短路径散射的蓝光，加上一束滤去了蓝光的直射日光。</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">What this is <em>not</em></h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">什么<em>不属于</em>此解释</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <ul class="en" lang="en">
          <li><strong>Clouds</strong>: droplet radii ~10–100 μm ⇒ x = 2πa/λ ~ O(10²–10⁴): Mie/geometric-optics regime with a wavelength-independent, strongly forward-peaked phase function and cross section approaching the geometric area ⇒ white (gray only by multiple-scattering/shadowing in thick layers).</li>
          <li><strong>The ocean</strong>: the sea's blue-green is an <em>absorption</em> story (intrinsic absorption of H₂O + dissolved organics removing red), not Rayleigh scattering of air.</li>
          <li><strong>Other skies</strong>: Mars — butterscotch from Mie-scattering dust and a blue sun (scattering out of the beam); Jupiter — yellowish from μm-scale ammonium-sulfide haze; the Moon — no sky at all.</li>
        </ul>
        <ul class="zh" lang="zh-CN">
          <li><strong>云</strong>：水滴半径 ~10–100 μm ⇒ x = 2πa/λ ~ O(10²–10⁴)：处于米氏/几何光学区，相函数与波长无关、强烈前向集中，总截面接近几何截面积 ⇒ 白色（只有在厚云层中，多次散射与遮挡效应才使其呈灰）。</li>
          <li><strong>海洋</strong>：海水的蓝绿色是一个<em>吸收</em>问题（H₂O 的本征吸收 + 溶解有机物的吸收滤去了红光），而非空气的瑞利散射。</li>
          <li><strong>其他天空</strong>：火星——尘埃的米氏散射使其天空呈奶黄色、太阳偏蓝（蓝光被散射出直射光束）；木星——微米级硫化铵霾使其天空偏黄；月球——根本没有天空。</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <h3 class="en" lang="en">TL;DR</h3>
        <h3 class="zh" lang="zh-CN">太长不看（TL;DR）</h3>
      </div>
      <div class="pair">
        <p class="en" lang="en">Sky color is single-scattered sunlight: dipole-induced molecular scattering with σ ∝ λ⁻⁴, τ_R ~ 0.1 across the visible, so the short-wavelength end of the solar spectrum dominates the scattered field; violet is suppressed by source-spectral falloff and the human visual system; and the whole thing becomes a red sun at large airmasses via exponential beam depletion.</p>
        <p class="zh" lang="zh-CN">天空的颜色就是单次散射的太阳光：由感应偶极子驱动的分子散射满足 σ ∝ λ⁻⁴，整个可见光波段 τ_R ~ 0.1，因此太阳光谱的短波端主导了散射场；紫色被源光谱向紫外的衰减和人眼视觉系统共同压制；而在大气质量很大时，直射光束按指数规律衰减，于是整幅景象变成了一轮红日。</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

